text: "# Examples — optimized profiles\n\nWorked profile specs showing the 3-second test, the searchable fields, and a goal-matched link —\nwith before/after contrast. Subject: a solo founder building a SaaS social scheduler. Voice is the\nblunt indie-founder voice; your output uses the loaded `voice.md` and `social-strategy.md` (goal →\nCTA).\n\n---\n\n## Before → after (the clarity fix)\n\n**Before (vague, leaks):**\n- Name field: \"Sam\"\n- Bio: \"founder ✨ | dreamer | building cool stuff | coffee addict ☕ | living the dream 🚀\"\n- Link: a Linktree with 14 links.\n\n→ Fails the 3-second test: who is this for? what does it do? why follow? A visitor leaves.\n\n**After (clear, converts):**\n- Name field: **\"Sam Lee | Social Media for Founders\"** (searchable keyword, not just \"Sam\")\n- Bio (≤150): **\"I help solo founders grow on social without burning out. / Building [Product] —\n  schedule everywhere from one place. / Free posting playbook ↓\"**\n- Link: **one** destination — the free playbook (the current goal), trackable.\n\n→ Passes the test instantly; the right visitor self-identifies and follows; one clear next step.\n\n---\n\n## Instagram spec\n\n- **Handle:** `@samlee` (consistent across platforms).\n- **Name field:** \"Sam Lee | Social for Founders\".\n- **Bio:** the \"after\" above.\n- **Profile pic:** clear headshot (face converts for a personal brand).\n- **Link:** free playbook (goal-matched); swap to the launch when campaigning.\n- **Highlights:** Start here · Proof · [Product] · FAQ.\n- **Pinned (grid):** intro Reel · best-performing teardown · the offer.\n\n## LinkedIn spec\n\n- **Headline:** \"Helping solo founders grow on social without burning out · Building [Product] ·\n  ex-[notable]\" (keywords + clarity, not just \"Founder\").\n- **About:** opens with the who/what/why (front-loaded), proof, CTA to the playbook.\n- **Banner brief:** value prop (\"Grow on social without burning out\") + [Product] logo + a subtle\n  CTA; legible text → hand to `tools/integrations/ideogram.md`.\n- **Featured:** the playbook + a top post.\n\n## TikTok spec (~80 chars)\n\n- **Bio:** \"Social media for founders. Building [Product]. Playbook ↓\" (niche + CTA, tight).\n- **Pinned:** 3 — an intro, a best performer, the offer.\n\n---\n\n## Contrast — what not to do\n\n- A name field that's just \"Sam\"; a bio of emojis and vibes; a 15-link junk-drawer hub; a stock-photo\n  banner; no pinned posts. Lots of visits, no follows — and the owner blames the algorithm.\n\n---\n\n## What the good specs share\n\n- **Searchable fields used** (name field / headline carry a niche keyword).\n- A **who/what/why bio** with **proof** and **one CTA**, on-voice, within the limit.\n- A **goal-matched link** (one destination or a hub leading with the priority).\n- **Pinned + highlights + banner** controlling the first impression.\n- **Consistent** handle/pic across platforms; **re-fit** bio per platform.\n- Advisory spec (ready to paste); no fabricated proof; no analytics claims.\n"
